    not_duplicate_of: []  # c83f
    pr_ref:  # c83f
    description: "Found while doing WI-runos (audit-findings 0021, Step 4). Measured on dev 544ac087ee with one-file repos:\n  kotlin: val k = System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); System.err.println(k)\n  scala:  val k = System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); System.err.println(k)\nBoth analyzers emit `calls kotlin|scala:external:0-0:println:external_symbol` and NO module_attr_ref for System.err (java emits `module_attr_ref ... System.out`). So java.lang.System.out / .err -- rowed logging since WI-runos and inherited by kotlin and scala through _CATALOG_PARENTS -- is never reached from a kotlin or scala FILE: host_secret -> logging reads confirmed_with_caveats, host_secret -> ipc likewise. A stdio write in kotlin or scala is seen by neither zone.\nThe spec already records the mechanism gap (\"Groovy and Kotlin have neither mechanism and emit no module_attr_ref edges\"); this is its measured consequence for the stdio rows, and scala is in it too.\nThe WI-runos A/B confirms: okhttp's and sbt's System.out crossings all came from .java files.\nFix shape: wire emit_module_attribute_refs into the kotlin and scala analyzers (WI-gapam wired the others), or reach it from the call through receiver typing (WI-dorus). Measure: kotlin/scala logging findings should only be ADDED."  # c83f
    fields: {}  # c83f
- op: discuss  # df3a
  at: '2026-09-30T23:23:16Z'  # df3a
  by: agent  # df3a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df3a
  clock: 2  # df3a
  nonce: df3a  # df3a
  message: "WI-dorus (PR #1341) typed java's System.out/err receivers as java.io.PrintStream and rowed PrintStream's writers (requires_target_kind: std_stream). kotlin and scala inherit those rows via _CATALOG_PARENTS, but their analyzers neither emit the System.out attribute ref nor type/stamp the receiver, so kotlin/scala stdio writes are still seen by no zone. Either fix (the attribute ref, or porting the java receiver typing + std_stream stamp) now lands on rows that exist."  # df3a
- op: discuss  # a9b2
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:09Z'  # a9b2
  by: agent  # a9b2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a9b2
  clock: 3  # a9b2
  nonce: a9b2  # a9b2
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT; one consequence corrected.\n- Fixture System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); System.err.println(k): kotlin and scala emit only `calls <lang>:external:0-0:println`, with no module_attr_ref and no receiver_type_hint. SECRET->LOGGING reads confirmed_with_caveats (rc 3; untyped_receiver, unknown_receiver_scope). Java control: java.io.PrintStream:println (io_target_kind std_stream) plus module_attr_ref java:System:0-0:System.err gives violated, precise. emit_module_attribute_refs is called from cpp, go, java, js_ts and rust, not kotlin or scala.\n- CORRECTION: host_secret->ipc is NOT affected. stdout/stderr are logging only (spec; audit 0021), and Java's own ipc claim reads confirmed. Only the logging zone loses the sink.\n- Related, not a duplicate: WI-jubim (kotlin/scala do not consume library signatures).\n- NOT CHECKED: which fix shape yields a finding. Java's violation came through the typed PrintStream.println call; whether a System.err attribute ref alone creates a sink is untested."  # a9b2
- op: discuss  # 8eba
  at: '2026-10-04T20:52:06Z'  # 8eba
  by: agent  # 8eba
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8eba
  clock: 4  # 8eba
  nonce: 8eba  # 8eba
  message: "WORK NOTE (concurrent run 10-03, stage 8b). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/rabum (local, NOT pushed), based on the stage-8 integration tip 2a98abb55d; commit b1c8437332.\n\nWhat: kotlin and scala now emit java's two records for System.out/err. (1) The println/print/... call on System.out/System.err (bare, or java.lang.System.*) is emitted <lang>:java.io.PrintStream:0-0:<m> with receiver_type_hint java.io.PrintStream and io_target_kind std_stream, so java.yaml's requires_target_kind: std_stream PrintStream rows apply. (2) System.in/out/err read as values become module_attr_ref <lang>:java.lang.System:0-0:java.lang.System.<f>:attribute through the SHARED base.emit_module_attribute_refs (attr_carrier stamped, anchored on the enclosing callable). Spellings, type, stamp, shadow rule (no local / project type / other import named System) and the alias map live once in jvm_implicit_imports; java's WI-dorus check now calls the same helper. The core helper gained generic options for tree-sitter-kotlin's fieldless nodes (@first / @last / @<type> pseudo-fields, carrier_argument_wrapper_kinds, attribute_names, backtick-quoted attributes), all defaulting to the old behaviour.\n\nBehavioral evidence: verify-claims on one-file fixtures, host_secret -> logging taint claim + logging must_not_exist claim. kotlin and scala System.err.println(secret) and System.out.print(secret): confirmed_with_caveats (untyped_receiver) -> violated, one finding each (the stream sink is subsumed by the println call, INV-hopib). Java control unchanged (violated). Controls (user object named out, local named out, project System, imported other System) emit no PrintStream type and no java.lang.System attr ref. Pinned by packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_jvm_stdio_writes.py and packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_attr_ref_unfielded_grammar.py.\n\nTests: red on 2a98abb55d 31 failed / 9 passed (new files only); targeted smart-test on the branch 24935 passed, 3 failed (my own assertion: scala names the method Main.go; fixed), coverage all files at 100%; rerun of both new files + test_signature_axis, test_module_key_axis, test_base, test_one_write_one_sink, test_jvm_library_signature_chains: 399 passed. Mutations (each watched red, then discarded): drop kotlin's std_stream stamp -> exactly the 3 kotlin typed-call tests red; scala attribute_names=None -> only the parameterless test red; project-type shadow ignored -> exactly the 2 project-System controls red; wrapper stepping off -> exactly the kotlin handed-on test and the core wrapper test red.\n\nANSWERS THE PREMISE AUDIT'S OPEN QUESTION: with the std_stream stamp removed (mutation 1) the kotlin secret test still read violated with one finding, so the System.err attribute ref alone does create a logging sink.\n\nCorpus (io-boundaries --include-tests, chains keyed by boundary/src/dst/primitive, before = 2a98abb55d, each arm printed its own code tree): okhttp +31 (kotlin: 15 System.out/err attrs, 14 PrintStream writes, 1 System.in ipc_recv, 1 external_potential PrintStream.sink -- okio's extension on System.out), detekt +8, sbt +96 (incl. 8 System.in ipc_recv), gatling +4; 0 removed in all four; java chains identical. 14 random additions read against source: all real System.out/err uses. Artifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/rabum/.\n\nNOT done / residuals: scala's own Predef.println and scala.Console writes have no row (filed separately -- a bare println(secret) reads confirmed with NO caveat); a stdio receiver held in a local (val e = System.err; e.println(k)) gets the attr ref but not the typed call, as in java. NOT measured: verify-claims on corpus repos.\nResidual filed: WI-tunul-rusir-katud-gibap-rorip-duhoz-lorav-musom (scala Predef println / scala.Console have no row; a bare println(secret) reads confirmed with no caveat)."  # 8eba
